# Every path needs review from the owner before it can merge into main.
#
# On a single-maintainer repo this cannot stop a bad change on its own — you
# are the reviewer. What it does buy is that a pull request from anyone else,
# including a compromised Dependabot run or an outside contributor, cannot
# merge without an explicit approval that names you. Branch protection has
# `require_code_owner_reviews` on, so this file is enforced, not advisory.

* @banagere

# Anything that can execute during CI or change what CI enforces. Called out
# separately from the catch-all so a diff touching the build gate is visibly a
# different class of change in the PR's review summary than a poem edit.
/.github/            @banagere
/.githooks/          @banagere
/scripts/            @banagere
/package.json        @banagere
/bun.lock            @banagere
/next.config.ts      @banagere
/.audit-baseline.json @banagere
